mQr.summary:
The QR patient forms system (migration 028) works like this. Each clinic has one live, never-expiring 10-character key (clinic_forms_key). Its only public door is /f/<key>/: a five-step form built from STEPS (About you, Your health, Your teeth, Cards, Consent). The patient signs by typing their name; there is exactly one general treatment consent (treatment-2026-09) plus the privacy tick. Submissions go only through the security-definer function patient_form_submit into patient_form, which is "not a patient". A form waits in /c/<slug>/patients/forms/ until someone with records.edit adds it as a new patient or to a patient on file (addAsNewPatient / addToPatient, which write patient, medical_history and patient_consent rows with channel 'form'), or dismisses it. A form nobody adds is purged after 30 days. The poster (/c/<slug>/patients/qr/) always encodes the same clinic-wide URL.

On a production server the forms stay closed while FORMS_PRIVACY_VERSIONS is empty. The reason: the notice in force (privacy-2026-09) does not name what the forms collect, and consent to sensitive personal information must be informed (RA 10173 s.13(a)).

A separate, closer match to "a consent for this procedure" already exists: visit_consent (035). The clinic ticks the treatment lines the dentist explained, hands the tablet over, and the patient signs by finger. But it needs an existing patient row and an appointment, and it has only the one general consent wording.

A per-patient, one-time link made after a staff checklist would need all of these, none of which the poster key has:
- its own token table (the poster key allows one live key per clinic and never expires);
- single use and an expiry;
- a staff author;
- a server-side record of which consent documents the checklist chose, and the clinic-filled content of each;
- procedure-specific consent versions (consent_version.kind allows only 'privacy' and 'treatment', and only one treatment version can be in force);
- a new definer function that checks the consents listed on the link instead of the fixed consent_treatment and consent_privacy keys;
- somewhere for drawn signatures other than the 24 KB answers blob;
- a new 4-page step definition with its own FORM_VERSION;
- new "used" and "expired" views;
- a new RESERVED path segment if it does not live under /f/;
- the same production privacy gate.

In this repository, docs/clinic-operations.md:59 already says consent should be per procedure and per visit: risk paragraphs chosen from the plan lines ticked, versioned, and signed by hand on the tablet.
